  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A Binary string SSS containing only 000s and 111s is cool if it contains exactly MMM different non-empty subsequences.\n\nNow your task is to find the number of inversions in NNN-th lexicographically maximum cool binary string.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line :\n\n\n\nIf there are at least NNN cool binary strings, the number of inversions in the NNN-th lexicographically largest binary string.\n−1-1−1 if there are less than NNN cool binary strings",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,M≤10121 \\le N, M \\le 10^{12}1≤N,M≤1012"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n3 3\n2 3\n19 10\n28 45\n158 189",
        "output": "0\n1\n-1\n16\n7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAll the good strings with exactly 333 distinct subsequences are listed below (in lexicographically descending order) :\n\n111\\text{111}111\n10\\text{10}10\n01\\text{01}01\n000\\text{000}000\n\nTest Case 1 : N=3N = 3N=3 and so the required string is 010101. This has 000 inversions.\nTest Case 2 : N=2N = 2N=2 and so the required string is 101010. This has 111 inversion.\nTest Case 3 : There are lesser than 191919 strings with number of distinct subsequences exactly 101010. Hence, the answer is −1-1−1."
      }
    ]
  },
